1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,840
Today we look at patterns made from dots. We

2
00:00:02,840 --> 00:00:06,140
will build lines, rectangles, squares and triangles, and then

3
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:10,640
use those patterns to calculate faster. Let's start with

4
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:11,371
a dot puzzle!

5
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:16,033
Here are six dots, scattered around. Can six dots

6
00:00:16,033 --> 00:00:21,537
make different shapes, without adding or removing a single

7
00:00:21,537 --> 00:00:23,923
dot? Watch: they line up in a row; then

8
00:00:23,923 --> 00:00:28,533
they become two rows of three; and then a

9
00:00:28,533 --> 00:00:31,412
triangle. Six equals two times three, and six is

10
00:00:31,412 --> 00:00:33,184
also one plus two plus three.

11
00:00:33,810 --> 00:00:38,850
Let's begin with the simplest pattern: a line. Two

12
00:00:38,850 --> 00:00:42,640
dots; one more makes three; one more makes four;

13
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:46,195
and one more makes five. Each step adds exactly

14
00:00:46,195 --> 00:00:49,650
one more dot, so we get two, three, four,

15
00:00:49,650 --> 00:00:51,201
five, and on and on.

16
00:00:51,827 --> 00:00:54,043
Now take six dots and arrange them as a

17
00:00:54,043 --> 00:00:58,327
rectangle: two rows, with three dots in each row.

18
00:00:58,327 --> 00:01:00,615
The first row has three dots, and the second

19
00:01:00,615 --> 00:01:02,811
row has three dots, so three plus three is

20
00:01:02,811 --> 00:01:04,947
six. Two rows of three is the same as

21
00:01:04,947 --> 00:01:09,578
two times three. A rectangle reveals multiplication!

22
00:01:10,073 --> 00:01:12,953
What if the rows and the columns are equal?

23
00:01:12,953 --> 00:01:15,813
Two rows of two give four dots. Three rows

24
00:01:15,813 --> 00:01:18,265
of three give nine dots. And four rows of

25
00:01:18,265 --> 00:01:22,093
four give sixteen dots. These are the square numbers:

26
00:01:22,093 --> 00:01:24,864
four, nine, sixteen, and so on.

27
00:01:25,437 --> 00:01:28,190
Now let's build triangles. A triangle starts with one

28
00:01:28,190 --> 00:01:31,877
dot, then a row of two: one plus two

29
00:01:31,877 --> 00:01:34,552
is three. Add a row of three, and we

30
00:01:34,552 --> 00:01:37,357
have one plus two plus three, which is six.

31
00:01:37,357 --> 00:01:41,005
What happens if we add one more row? Four

32
00:01:41,005 --> 00:01:43,146
dots in the bottom row give one plus two

33
00:01:43,146 --> 00:01:46,157
plus three plus four, which is ten. So the

34
00:01:46,157 --> 00:01:49,788
triangular numbers are three, six, ten, and so on.

35
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:53,390
Patterns can make calculations easier too. Look at two

36
00:01:53,390 --> 00:01:56,487
hundred ninety six plus nine. Nine is almost ten,

37
00:01:56,487 --> 00:01:58,834
because nine is ten minus one. So we add

38
00:01:58,834 --> 00:02:02,110
ten, and then take one away. For subtraction, two

39
00:02:02,110 --> 00:02:05,981
hundred ninety six minus nine: take away ten, and

40
00:02:05,981 --> 00:02:09,690
add one back. Now with ninety nine, which is

41
00:02:09,690 --> 00:02:13,690
one hundred minus one. Two hundred ninety six plus

42
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:17,330
ninety nine: add one hundred, then take one away.

43
00:02:17,330 --> 00:02:21,970
And two hundred ninety six minus ninety nine: subtract

44
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:23,881
one hundred, then add one back.

45
00:02:24,433 --> 00:02:27,773
The same idea works for multiplication. Sixty five times

46
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:30,890
ninety nine. Ninety nine is one hundred minus one.

47
00:02:30,890 --> 00:02:33,847
So we write sixty five times, one hundred minus

48
00:02:33,847 --> 00:02:36,713
one, in a bracket. Now multiply sixty five by

49
00:02:36,713 --> 00:02:39,893
both terms: sixty five times one hundred is six

50
00:02:39,893 --> 00:02:42,982
thousand five hundred, and sixty five times one is

51
00:02:42,982 --> 00:02:46,273
sixty five. Six thousand five hundred minus sixty five

52
00:02:46,273 --> 00:02:49,004
is six thousand four hundred and thirty five.

53
00:02:49,627 --> 00:02:52,760
Here is a practical example. A packet holds twenty

54
00:02:52,760 --> 00:02:56,610
five stickers, and we have forty six packets. Twenty

55
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:59,177
five is twenty plus five. So we calculate forty

56
00:02:59,177 --> 00:03:02,774
six times, twenty plus five, in a bracket. That

57
00:03:02,774 --> 00:03:04,927
is forty six times twenty, which is nine hundred

58
00:03:04,927 --> 00:03:07,647
and twenty, plus forty six times five, which is

59
00:03:07,647 --> 00:03:10,907
two hundred and thirty. Nine hundred and twenty plus

60
00:03:10,907 --> 00:03:13,967
two hundred and thirty is one thousand, one hundred

61
00:03:13,967 --> 00:03:15,458
and fifty stickers.

62
00:03:16,097 --> 00:03:20,172
Your turn! Two questions. First, here is a triangle

63
00:03:20,172 --> 00:03:22,977
of six dots: how many dots do we need

64
00:03:22,977 --> 00:03:26,577
for the next triangle? Second: sixty five times nine

65
00:03:26,577 --> 00:03:29,697
hundred and ninety nine. Pause the video and try

66
00:03:29,697 --> 00:03:30,508
both.

67
00:03:35,570 --> 00:03:38,375
Let's check. The next triangle needs a bottom row

68
00:03:38,375 --> 00:03:41,230
of four dots, so one plus two plus three

69
00:03:41,230 --> 00:03:45,110
plus four is ten. And for the multiplication, nine

70
00:03:45,110 --> 00:03:48,110
hundred and ninety nine is one thousand minus one.

71
00:03:48,110 --> 00:03:51,439
Sixty five times one thousand is sixty five thousand,

72
00:03:51,439 --> 00:03:55,873
and we subtract sixty five: sixty four thousand, nine

73
00:03:55,873 --> 00:03:57,741
hundred and thirty five.

74
00:03:58,380 --> 00:04:01,118
Let's recap. Dots can make a line, a rectangle,

75
00:04:01,118 --> 00:04:03,229
a square or a triangle. The square numbers are

76
00:04:03,229 --> 00:04:06,671
four, nine and sixteen, and the triangular numbers are

77
00:04:06,671 --> 00:04:10,280
three, six and ten. For quick calculations, remember that

78
00:04:10,280 --> 00:04:14,180
nine is ten minus one, and ninety nine is

79
00:04:14,180 --> 00:04:18,460
one hundred minus one. See the pattern, and simplify

80
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:22,788
the calculation. Thank you for watching! See you in

81
00:04:22,788 --> 00:04:24,031
the next lesson!
